  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow is a reusable Docker image publishing workflow. Every matrix job explicitly sets `fail-fast: false`, indicating each platform build is required, which matches the P-LIT-FAIL-FAST contraindication \"Every matrix outcome is required\" for multi-arch publishing. There are no dependency-installation steps (npm/pip/etc.) to cache, so P-LIT-GHA-CACHE does not apply. There are no Bazel builds, so the Bazel patterns do not apply. There are no test steps to select or prioritize. There is no representative successful-duration history to derive a job timeout, so P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT's precondition is unmet. The workflow is deployment-like (publishes images), so P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE is contraindicated. No evidence-supported optimization safely applies while preserving build and test coverage.",
  "evidence_ids": ["pattern:P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "pattern:P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "pattern:P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "pattern:P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE"]
}
